  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.1: explicit numeric narrowing family — toByte/toInt16/toUint32/... plus toXxxWrap (two's-complement) and toXxxClamp (saturating) variants for all fixed-width int types; toReal; toFloat32/toFloat64 under the float-family dialect. Overflow semantics live in the function name, independent of the dialect overflow flag: `counter:byte = (counter + 1).toByte()`. Function-name aliases mirror type-keyword aliases (toByte≡toUint8, toInt≡toInt32, toUint≡toUint32).",
